-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 9, RULES 1 TO 9: case conferences, the single application pending trial.  Part roc2, layer 1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT (full statement in NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc2)").
--   JUST TRUE    the Rule gives the power, the duty or the permission on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the Rule says no in its own words: a failed "if" or "where" (marginal reading (a), ruled
--                as the status quo), a flat negative, a stated period that has been missed (ruling of
--                2026-11-05, (a)), or a "must" that has not been met.
--   NOTHING      the Rule does not answer: a power or prohibition limited by its own wording and the case
--                is outside the limit, a list that is not closed, silence, or a fact that lives elsewhere.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every answer here is subject to O 3 r 2(1) (roc1): the Court's discretion to order otherwise.
-- The count of a period is O 3 r 3 (roc1).  Each period function takes `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rule 1 -- general matters`
-- ===========================================================================

-- The two periods of paragraph (1): 8 weeks where the defendant is to be served in Singapore, 12 weeks
-- where the originating claim or originating application is to be served out of Singapore.
-- src:731 | 1. —(1) A case conference is to be held — ( a )
-- src:732 | in a case where the defendant is to be served in Singapore — 8 weeks after the originating claim or originating application is issued; or
@ref O 9 r 1(1)(a) (src:731-732)
`o 9 r 1(1)(a) eight weeks` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 8
    `period unit` IS Weeks
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:733 | ( b )
-- src:734 | in a case where an originating claim or originating application is to be served out of Singapore — 12 weeks after the originating claim or originating application is issued.
@ref O 9 r 1(1)(b) (src:733-734)
`o 9 r 1(1)(b) twelve weeks` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 12
    `period unit` IS Weeks
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:731 | 1. —(1) A case conference is to be held — ( a )
-- src:732 | in a case where the defendant is to be served in Singapore — 8 weeks after the originating claim or originating application is issued; or
-- src:733 | ( b )
-- src:734 | in a case where an originating claim or originating application is to be served out of Singapore — 12 weeks after the originating claim or originating application is issued.
@ref O 9 r 1(1) (src:731-734)
GIVEN `place of service` IS A `Place of service`
GIVETH A Period
`o 9 r 1(1) the period before the case conference` MEANS
    CONSIDER `place of service`
    WHEN `Served in Singapore` THEN `o 9 r 1(1)(a) eight weeks`
    WHEN `Served out of Singapore` THEN `o 9 r 1(1)(b) twelve weeks`

-- The Rule itself fixes the day ("is to be held ... 8 weeks after ... is issued"), so the day is calendar
-- arithmetic on the issue date: 8 weeks is 56 days, 12 weeks is 84 days (fork F-O9-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:731 | 1. —(1) A case conference is to be held — ( a )
-- src:732 | in a case where the defendant is to be served in Singapore — 8 weeks after the originating claim or originating application is issued; or
-- src:733 | ( b )
-- src:734 | in a case where an originating claim or originating application is to be served out of Singapore — 12 weeks after the originating claim or originating application is issued.
@ref O 9 r 1(1) (src:731-734)
GIVEN `place of service` IS A `Place of service`
      `the day the originating claim or originating application is issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`o 9 r 1(1) the day on which the case conference is to be held` MEANS
    `the day the originating claim or originating application is issued` PLUS (7 TIMES (`o 9 r 1(1) the period before the case conference` `place of service`)'s `period length`)

-- src:731 | 1. —(1) A case conference is to be held — ( a )
-- src:732 | in a case where the defendant is to be served in Singapore — 8 weeks after the originating claim or originating application is issued; or
-- src:733 | ( b )
-- src:734 | in a case where an originating claim or originating application is to be served out of Singapore — 12 weeks after the originating claim or originating application is issued.
@ref O 9 r 1(1) (src:731-734)
GIVEN `place of service` IS A `Place of service`
      `the day the originating claim or originating application is issued` IS A DATE
      `the day the case conference is held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 1(1) the case conference is held at the time stated in paragraph (1)` MEANS
    IF `the day the case conference is held` EQUALS `o 9 r 1(1) the day on which the case conference is to be held` `place of service` `the day the originating claim or originating application is issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "8 weeks after the originating claim or originating application is issued" / "12 weeks after" (a time the text fixes in its own words; paragraph (2) lets the Court hold one earlier or later)

-- paragraph (2): at the request of any party, or on the Court's own accord.
-- src:735 | (2) The Court may hold a case conference earlier or later than the time stated in paragraph (1) at the request of any party or on its own accord.
@ref O 9 r 1(2) (src:735)
GIVEN `a party asks for the case conference to be held earlier or later` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court acts on its own accord` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 1(2) the Court may hold a case conference earlier or later than the time stated in paragraph (1)` MEANS
    IF `a party asks for the case conference to be held earlier or later` OR `the Court acts on its own accord`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the request of any party or on its own accord" [marginal-b]

-- paragraphs (3) and (5): "at any stage of the proceedings, including appeals".
DECLARE `o 9 r 1(3) stage of the proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 1(3) before trial`
    `o 9 r 1(3) at trial`
    `o 9 r 1(3) after judgment`
    `o 9 r 1(3) on appeal`

-- src:736 | (3) The Court may hold as many case conferences as the Court thinks appropriate and at any stage of the proceedings, including appeals.
@ref O 9 r 1(3) (src:736)
GIVEN stage IS A `o 9 r 1(3) stage of the proceedings`
      `the Court thinks the number of case conferences appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 1(3) the Court may hold a case conference at this stage of the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the Court thinks the number of case conferences appropriate`
    THEN
        CONSIDER stage
        WHEN `o 9 r 1(3) before trial` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 1(3) at trial` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 1(3) after judgment` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 1(3) on appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as many case conferences as the Court thinks appropriate" [marginal-b]

-- paragraph (4): the Registrar conducts the case conference as a general rule, and may refer any matter at
-- any time to the assigned Judge or, if there is none, to any Judge.
DECLARE `o 9 r 1(4) the Judge to whom a matter is referred` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 1(4) the assigned Judge in that action`
    `o 9 r 1(4) any Judge`

-- src:737 | (4) As a general rule, the Registrar is to conduct the case conference but the Registrar may refer any matter at any time to the assigned Judge in that action or, if there is none, to any Judge.
@ref O 9 r 1(4) (src:737)
GIVEN `the Registrar has referred the matter to a Judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Decision maker`
`o 9 r 1(4) who conducts the case conference` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has referred the matter to a Judge`
    THEN `A Judge`
    ELSE `The Registrar` -- "As a general rule, the Registrar is to conduct the case conference"

-- src:737 | (4) As a general rule, the Registrar is to conduct the case conference but the Registrar may refer any matter at any time to the assigned Judge in that action or, if there is none, to any Judge.
@ref O 9 r 1(4) (src:737)
GIVEN `there is an assigned Judge in that action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `o 9 r 1(4) the Judge to whom a matter is referred`
`o 9 r 1(4) the Registrar may refer a matter at any time to` MEANS
    IF `there is an assigned Judge in that action`
    THEN `o 9 r 1(4) the assigned Judge in that action`
    ELSE `o 9 r 1(4) any Judge`

-- src:738 | (5) The powers in this Order may be exercised by the Court at any stage of the proceedings, including appeals.
@ref O 9 r 1(5) (src:738)
GIVEN stage IS A `o 9 r 1(3) stage of the proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 1(5) the Court may exercise the powers in Order 9 at this stage of the proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER stage
    WHEN `o 9 r 1(3) before trial` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 9 r 1(3) at trial` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 9 r 1(3) after judgment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 9 r 1(3) on appeal` THEN JUST TRUE

-- The seam asked by O 1 r 3(1) "case conference" ("means a case conference as described in Order 9, Rule 1",
-- text line 93): a meeting held under paragraph (1), (2) or (3).  Rule 1 does not otherwise describe the meeting,
-- so any other meeting is not covered.
-- src:731 | 1. —(1) A case conference is to be held — ( a )
-- src:732 | in a case where the defendant is to be served in Singapore — 8 weeks after the originating claim or originating application is issued; or
-- src:733 | ( b )
-- src:734 | in a case where an originating claim or originating application is to be served out of Singapore — 12 weeks after the originating claim or originating application is issued.
-- src:735 | (2) The Court may hold a case conference earlier or later than the time stated in paragraph (1) at the request of any party or on its own accord.
-- src:736 | (3) The Court may hold as many case conferences as the Court thinks appropriate and at any stage of the proceedings, including appeals.
@ref O 9 r 1 (src:731-736)
GIVEN `the meeting is held at the time stated in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is held earlier or later under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is one of the case conferences the Court holds under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 1 the meeting is a case conference as described` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is held at the time stated in paragraph (1)` OR `the meeting is held earlier or later under paragraph (2)` OR `the meeting is one of the case conferences the Court holds under paragraph (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): Rule 1 says when a case conference "is to be held" and does not otherwise say what a case conference is

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rule 2 -- purpose of case conference`
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `o 9 r 2 a thing the Court is to do at a case conference` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 2 take control of the proceedings`
    `o 9 r 2 set the timelines`
    `o 9 r 2 give directions for the proceedings`

-- src:740 | 2. At a case conference, the Court is to take control of and set the timelines and give directions for the proceedings.
@ref O 9 r 2 (src:740)
GIVEN thing IS A `o 9 r 2 a thing the Court is to do at a case conference`
      `it is a case conference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 2 the Court is to do this` MEANS
    IF `it is a case conference`
    THEN
        CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `o 9 r 2 take control of the proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 2 set the timelines` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 2 give directions for the proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "At a case conference" [marginal-b]

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rule 3 -- non-disclosure`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:742 | 3. Subject to the law governing the admissibility of evidence at trial, any communication made in the course of a case conference in any action or proceedings must not be disclosed to the Court conducting the trial of the action or proceedings if such communication — ( a )
-- src:743 | has been stated by any of the parties to the action or proceedings to be “confidential” or “without prejudice”; or
-- src:744 | ( b )
-- src:745 | has been marked by the Registrar or Judge (as the case may be) as being “confidential” or “without prejudice”.
@ref O 9 r 3 (src:742-745)
GIVEN `the law governing the admissibility of evidence at trial otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication was made in the course of a case conference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a party has stated it to be confidential or without prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar or Judge has marked it confidential or without prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 3 the communication may be disclosed to the Court conducting the trial` MEANS
    IF `the law governing the admissibility of evidence at trial otherwise provides`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to the law governing the admissibility of evidence at trial"
    ELSE
        IF `the communication was made in the course of a case conference` AND (`a party has stated it to be confidential or without prejudice` OR `the Registrar or Judge has marked it confidential or without prejudice`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be disclosed to the Court conducting the trial" (flat negative, ruling N2)
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition reaches a communication "stated by any of the parties ... to be" or "marked by the Registrar or Judge as" "confidential" or "without prejudice" [marginal-b]

