§ `Order 9, Rule 4 -- absence of parties`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:747 | 4. —(1) If no party attends the case conference or if the claimant is absent, the Court may dismiss the action. (2) If the claimant attends the case conference but the defendant is absent, the Court may give judgment for the claimant upon proof of service of the originating claim or originating application on the defendant.
@ref O 9 r 4(1) (src:747)
GIVEN `no party attends the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is absent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 4(1) the Court may dismiss the action` MEANS
    IF `no party attends the case conference` OR `the claimant is absent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no party attends the case conference or if the claimant is absent" [marginal-a]

-- src:747 | 4. —(1) If no party attends the case conference or if the claimant is absent, the Court may dismiss the action. (2) If the claimant attends the case conference but the defendant is absent, the Court may give judgment for the claimant upon proof of service of the originating claim or originating application on the defendant.
@ref O 9 r 4(2) (src:747)
GIVEN `the claimant attends the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant is absent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proof of service of the originating claim or originating application on the defendant is given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 4(2) the Court may give judgment for the claimant` MEANS
    IF `the claimant attends the case conference` AND `the defendant is absent`
    THEN
        IF `proof of service of the originating claim or originating application on the defendant is given`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon proof of service" (an "upon" read as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05: "when", "upon" and "whenever" count as "where") [marginal-a]
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the claimant attends the case conference but the defendant is absent" [marginal-a]

-- src:748 | (3) The Court may set aside or vary the dismissal or default judgment on proof that there were valid reasons for the absence of the defaulting party.
@ref O 9 r 4(3) (src:748)
GIVEN `the dismissal or default judgment was given under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there were valid reasons for the absence of the defaulting party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 4(3) the Court may set aside or vary the dismissal or default judgment` MEANS
    IF `the dismissal or default judgment was given under this Rule`
    THEN
        IF `there were valid reasons for the absence of the defaulting party`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on proof that there were valid reasons for the absence of the defaulting party" (read as the same condition as "upon proof of service" in paragraph (2), fork F-O9-6; ruling of 2026-11-05 on "upon") [marginal-a]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the dismissal or default judgment" of paragraphs (1) and (2) only; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

