    IF `the Court extended time for the defendant to serve the defence` AND `the defendant did not serve the defence within the extended time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "failing which the defendant is deemed not to have served a defence" (the deeming is conditional on the failure, read as an "if") [marginal-a]

@ref O 9 r 6(3) (src:761)
GIVEN `the Court extended time for the defendant to serve the defence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant did not serve the defence within the extended time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 6(3) the claimant is entitled to judgment under paragraph (1)` MEANS
    `o 9 r 6(3) the defendant is deemed not to have served a defence` `the Court extended time for the defendant to serve the defence` `the defendant did not serve the defence within the extended time`

-- src:762 | (4) This Rule applies, with the necessary modifications, to a claimant’s default to serve a defence to the defendant’s counterclaim.
@ref O 9 r 6(4) (src:762)
GIVEN `the default is by a claimant in serving a defence to the defendant's counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 6(4) this Rule applies with the necessary modifications` MEANS
    IF `the default is by a claimant in serving a defence to the defendant's counterclaim`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a claimant's default to serve a defence to the defendant's counterclaim"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rule 7 -- challenges to jurisdiction of Court`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:764 | 7. —(1) If both the claimant and defendant attend the case conference and — ( a )
-- src:765 | a defence has been filed and served in the case of an originating claim; or
-- src:766 | ( b )
-- src:767 | the defendant’s affidavit has been filed and served in the case of an originating application,
-- src:768 | the Court must first deal with any objection to its jurisdiction.
@ref O 9 r 7(1) (src:764-768)
GIVEN `the claimant and the defendant both attend the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in an originating claim, a defence has been filed and served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in an originating application, the defendant's affidavit has been filed and served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 7(1) the Court must first deal with any objection to its jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `the claimant and the defendant both attend the case conference` AND (`in an originating claim, a defence has been filed and served` OR `in an originating application, the defendant's affidavit has been filed and served`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If both the claimant and defendant attend the case conference and" a defence or the defendant's affidavit "has been filed and served" [marginal-a]

DECLARE `o 9 r 7(2) a direction the Court must give` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 7(2)(a) direct the defendant to file and serve the application and affidavit within 14 days after the date of the case conference`
    `o 9 r 7(2)(b) direct the claimant to file and serve any affidavit in reply within 14 days thereafter`
    `o 9 r 7(2)(c) fix the hearing of the application no later than 14 days after all affidavits have been filed and served`

-- src:769 | (2) If the defendant is challenging the jurisdiction of the Court, the Court must — ( a )
-- src:770 | direct the defendant to file and serve the necessary application with supporting affidavit within 14 days after the date of the case conference;
-- src:771 | ( b )
-- src:772 | direct the claimant to file and serve any affidavit in reply within 14 days thereafter, with no further affidavits to be filed without the Court’s approval; and
-- src:773 | ( c )
-- src:774 | unless the Court otherwise orders, fix the hearing of the application on a date no later than 14 days after all affidavits have been filed and served.
@ref O 9 r 7(2) (src:769-774)
GIVEN `the defendant is challenging the jurisdiction of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      direction IS A `o 9 r 7(2) a direction the Court must give`
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 7(2) the Court must give this direction` MEANS
    IF `the defendant is challenging the jurisdiction of the Court`
    THEN
        CONSIDER direction
        WHEN `o 9 r 7(2)(a) direct the defendant to file and serve the application and affidavit within 14 days after the date of the case conference` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 7(2)(b) direct the claimant to file and serve any affidavit in reply within 14 days thereafter` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 7(2)(c) fix the hearing of the application no later than 14 days after all affidavits have been filed and served` THEN
            IF `the Court otherwise orders`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court otherwise orders"
            ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the defendant is challenging the jurisdiction of the Court" [marginal-a]

