`o 9 r 9(10) fourteen days before the commencement of the trial` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `Before the anchor`

-- The period in which paragraph (10) forbids an application starts 14 days before the trial begins and ends
-- when the Court has determined the merits.  Outside that period the paragraph says nothing about whether an
-- application may be taken out, so the answer is NOTHING (fork F-O9-3: a period that bounds a prohibition is a
-- scope limit, ruling (c), and not a period in which a duty runs, ruling (a)).
-- src:844 | (10) No application may be taken out during the period starting 14 days before the commencement of the trial and ending when the Court has determined the merits of the action, except in a special case and with the trial Judge’s approval.
@ref O 9 r 9(10) (src:844)
