      `o 3 r 3 the day 14 days before the commencement of the trial` IS A DATE
      `the Court has determined the merits of the action by the date of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial Judge approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 9(10) an application may be taken out` MEANS
    IF `the date of the application` AT LEAST `o 3 r 3 the day 14 days before the commencement of the trial` AND (NOT `the Court has determined the merits of the action by the date of the application`)
    THEN
        IF `it is a special case` AND `the trial Judge approves`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No application may be taken out during the period starting 14 days before the commencement of the trial and ending when the Court has determined the merits of the action, except in a special case and with the trial Judge's approval" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is for "the period starting 14 days before the commencement of the trial and ending when the Court has determined the merits"; outside it paragraph (10) is silent [marginal-b]

